# Build context is the repo root (see docker/Dockerfile's COPY paths and the
# "Building and publishing the image" section of README.md) so that the
# Dockerfile can pull docker/report-theme's favicons straight from
# assets/favicon/ instead of keeping a second, hand-synced copy under
# docker/report-theme/favicon/. Everything below either isn't needed inside
# the image or is actively large/slow to hash-and-send to the Docker daemon
# on every build — mirrors the "why" reasoning in .gitignore, not its exact
# contents (e.g. CLAUDE.md is git-ignored but harmless/tiny to send; not
# worth listing here).
.git/
/Archi/
/spikes/
